WEBVTT

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:11.294
One payment, no subscription. Review the price shown on screen. Use a promotional code only if you have a valid one. The current price and available methods are confirmed at payment.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:25.047
Your style, in your own words. Describe pace, interests, breaks, mobility or important needs. We keep the original example text. This field is optional: add only what matters.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:30.797
Ask Info Chat for help. Ask about areas, transport, food or ideas for the cities in your route. Getting help is optional; you can continue without it.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:45.047
Ideas for your must-sees. This example asks for must-sees in each city. Use the response as guidance for your preferences. You do not need to know every place: you can let ITBMO decide.

00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:58.547
Recommendations with context. Info Chat considers the cities in the route. You can ask for guidance for the whole trip. These are example questions; choose which suggestions to keep.

00:00:58.549 --> 00:01:17.412
Personalize Madrid. Choose your lodging status, local transport and pace. Add must-sees if you already know them. Without lodging set, ITBMO chooses a base area. For transport, you can choose “Recommend”.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:36.262
Personalize Barcelona. Adjust each city separately. We keep the original places and choices from this example. Name or address, bookings, exclusions and notes are optional where indicated.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:44.284
Your itinerary language. Choose the language of your result. It can differ from the language of the interface. The example selection is preserved.

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:50.047
Now generate your itinerary. When everything is ready, press the button to create the itinerary. The example details remain the same throughout the demonstration.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:58.450
ITBMO prepares your trip. Cities, times, transfers and priorities are organized. Keep this tab open during generation. It normally takes a few minutes; complex trips may need longer.
